% ============================================================================
% histo-recall.query.adj — a worked recall query over the histology-finding library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape an LLM (or a clinician) produces to ANSWER a "what does this smear/histology
% finding suggest?" question: it states no pathology fact — it only `import`s the grounded
% library and asks binding queries. The native adj-lang engine resolves each `?` against
% the imported `relate` edges and returns the binding + the citing clause's
% source/locator/trust. All knowledge is in the library; none is here. (A finding that
% points to several conditions binds multiple answers — each with its own citation.)
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli histo-recall.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "histo-edges.adj"

? seen_in(reed_sternberg_cells, $Condition)   % expect hodgkin_lymphoma
? seen_in(howell_jolly_bodies, $Condition)    % expect asplenia / megaloblastic_anemia
? seen_in(heinz_bodies, $Condition)           % expect g6pd_deficiency / methemoglobinemia
? seen_in(auer_rods, $Condition)              % expect acute_promyelocytic_leukemia (backfill)
? seen_in(psammoma_bodies, $Condition)        % expect meningioma (backfill)
